course: dictionary
lesson: 9852
title: Sycophantic: fake praise to get something
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A sycophant is someone who praises and agrees with a powerful or important person too much, in a fake way, to get something from them. «Being too keen to agree and praise is called being "sycophantic".» Look at the clues: too keen, too much, fake, and to get something. Those words show you the meaning.
explain: Imagine a king's servant who tells the king he is the cleverest ruler ever, even when the king is clearly wrong. The reader knows the servant is not being honest. «A long word for a yes-man is "sycophantic".» A yes-man always says yes to the boss, whatever he really thinks.
explain: At school you may hear "teacher's pet", "suck-up" or "crawler" for a similar idea. Honest kindness is different: a true friend tells you the truth politely, even when it is hard to hear. Sycophancy is a kind of dishonesty, because the praise is not real.
fact: Sycophantic is an adjective. A sycophant is the person, and sycophancy is the behaviour.
fact: «Sycophantic» means praising and agreeing with a powerful or important person too much, in a fake way, to get something from them.
fact: Clue words in the meaning: too much, fake, and to get something.
fact: Informal words for a sycophant include "teacher's pet", "suck-up" (US) and "crawler" (UK and Australia).
fact: "Brown-noser" is rude slang, so do not use it.
exercise: Ravi laughs at every joke the head teacher makes and says she is the best head ever, just to get a good report. What is Ravi being? | Lazy | Curious | Brave | *Sycophantic
exercise: What does sycophantic mean? | Lost in thought about the weather | Running very fast to win a race | *Praising a powerful person too much, in a fake way, to get something | Telling the truth even when it is hard
exercise: Which informal word, used in the UK, is close in meaning to sycophant? | *Crawler | Honest friend | Night owl | Good sport
test: «A long word for a yes-man is "sycophantic".» Which word best fits? The yes-man always agreed with the boss, even when he was wrong, so he was being ____. | barely | *sycophantic | ancient | luminous
test: Why is sycophancy a kind of dishonesty? | Because it always tells the truth | Because it is always rude to other people | *Because the praise is fake and not what the person really thinks | Because it makes everyone laugh
exam: A friend says your drawing is brilliant only because you are the class captain, not because they think so. What is this? | *Sycophancy | Curiosity | Patience | Honest kindness
